    <meta name='description' content='Repro for a spec question: the X3D 4.1 draft GaussianSplats node holds its data inline. X_ITE 16.4.3 also loads a 3D Gaussian splatting PLY through a plain Inline url. knot-splats.ply holds a gold trefoil knot with an arrow pointing to +Y in the PLY frame. Left: the PLY by Inline url, as X_ITE loads it (it adds a 180 degree turn about X, the y-down convention of 3DGS training data, so the arrow points down). Right: the same Inline inside a Transform that turns it back. A standard X3D tool sees an Inline to a file of a non-X3D type.'/>
